--
-- WHAT IT DOES. Upserts the post into website.blog_posts by slug, in one transaction.
-- A re-run rewrites title, excerpt, content, author, tags, is_english, is_tech and
-- time_required_minutes and bumps updated_at. It never touches published, published_at,
-- view_count, is_featured or created_at, so a re-run does not re-date a post, reset its
-- views, or re-publish one somebody unpublished on purpose.
--
-- THE GUARD. If a row created before 2026-11-21 already holds one of these slugs, it
-- is someone else's post: the DO block raises, ON_ERROR_STOP stops psql, and the
-- transaction rolls back with nothing written.
--
-- APPLY on the box, from /opt/birjob, and record it in the same paste (&& so a failed
-- apply is never recorded; deploy/check-migrations.sh explains why). Load .env.hetzner
-- first: compose interpolates its variables, and the box's .env holds only APP_TAG.
--
--   cd /opt/birjob && set -a && . ./.env.hetzner && set +a
--   docker compose exec -T db psql -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -U birjob_owner -d birjob \
--     < prisma/migrations/2026-11-21_blog_post_bus_networks_26_cities.sql && \
--   docker compose exec -T db psql -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -U birjob_owner -d birjob -c \
--     "INSERT INTO website._migrations (name) VALUES ('2026-11-21_blog_post_bus_networks_26_cities.sql') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING"
--
-- No code depends on these rows, so the order relative to a deploy does not matter for
-- correctness; the deploy gate simply refuses to deploy until this is recorded.
--
-- AFTER APPLYING. The URL renders on their first request (blog/[slug] has
-- dynamicParams). The /blog listing picks them up within its 5-minute cache, the
-- sitemap within the hour. Do not open the URL BEFORE applying: the page reads its
-- row through a 24-hour data cache tagged 'blog-posts', so an early request can pin a
-- not-found for the slug. The same cache holds the old text after a re-run that
-- changes a post. Either way, saving any post in the admin Blog tab revalidates the tag;
-- otherwise it expires within 24 hours.
--
-- INVERSE (content preserved, as in 2026-07-26c_unpublish_personal_blog_posts.sql):
--   UPDATE website.blog_posts SET published = FALSE WHERE slug IN ('bus-networks-26-cities-open-timetables');
--
-- VERIFY (run separately; expect one row, published, is_english true):
--   SELECT slug, published, published_at, is_english, is_tech, time_required_minutes,
--          length(content) FROM website.blog_posts WHERE slug IN ('bus-networks-26-cities-open-timetables')
--    ORDER BY published_at DESC;

